<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#grand-pensionary">Glossary</a> · Term · office</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand Pensionary</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Raadpensionaris</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Grand Pensionary was the leading official of the province of Holland in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>, its chief legal adviser and spokesman in the States General, and often the effective director of the Republic's policy. Holders included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johan-de-witt">Johan de Witt</a>. The office, which replaced the earlier Land's Advocate, was revived for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rutger-jan-schimmelpenninck">Rutger Jan Schimmelpenninck</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavian-republic">Batavian Republic</a> in 1805.</p></div>
